th consume  have a cup of your favorite fermented  vegetables or two ounces of your  favorite fermented liquid  now if fermented foods are completely  new to your system you may experience  some mild to moderate symptoms which is  completely natural and healthy for your  body this include gas breakout headaches  and more but don't worry  nothing wrong is happening guys in fact  only the good things are happening  because your body is getting rid of  toxins so give your body time to adjust  and also adapt the ferment of food are  replacing those toxins with beneficial  life enhancing bacteria which will  eventually make you feel and look good  so as your body slowly adjust you can  add one more additional serving so add  another half a cup of fermented  vegetables or 2 ounces of your favorite  fermented liquid into two of your meals  in a day again  moderation is key to good health ok you  don't have to spend lots of money on  fermented foods or drinks in fact you  can make them at home it is really  simple it requires very little  ingredients but a lot of patience so I'm  gonna share with you three fermented  vegetables to get you started let's  start with a sauerkraut only two  ingredients 3 pounds of green cabbage  shredded and about one and a half  tablespoons of pink Himalayan salt  simply combined at the cabbage and salt  begin working the salt into the cabbage  by massaging and squeezing the cabbage  with your hands until the cabbage is  watery and limp this will take about  five to ten minutes so be patient and  work of those biceps then grab handfuls  of the cabbage and pack them into your  just pour any liquid released by the  cabbage into the jar then place one of  the larger outer leaves of the cabbage  over the surface to cover the strata  cabbage to where the cabbage down slip  in a smaller jar weighted with stones or  pebbles you want to make sure that the  cabbage is fully submerged beneath its  liquid cover the mouth of the jar with a  cloth to make 